    "caveats": [
      "Verify the retinal arteriole shear target (1.5 Pa / 15 dyn/cm²) against the specific literature source you are recapitulating; reported first-order retinal arteriole values span ~10-20 dyn/cm² (1-2 Pa).",
      "The registry maps retinal microvascular endothelium to HUVEC physiology; if you use primary human retinal microvascular endothelial cells (HRMEC), confirm BSL-2 handling and their specific shear tolerance before exposing them to the high 1.5 Pa shear.",
      "Confirm the syringe pump can deliver 60 µL/min steadily; the ~600 Pa pressure drop is well within range but verify tubing/connector integrity at this flow.",
      "Culture medium viscosity assumed 1e-3 Pa·s (water-like); if using a serum-supplemented or high-protein medium, re-measure viscosity and recompute the flow for the exact shear.",
      "Seed ~1200-1600 cells on the 0.08 cm² channel floor and allow attachment/confluence before starting perfusion; verify monolayer integrity under the high shear.",
      "High shear (1.5 Pa) may induce endothelial alignment and junctional remodeling; include a low-shear control channel (e.g. 0.1-0.5 Pa) to isolate shear-dependent effects."
    ]
